# Optional. You do NOT need this file to build a working bundle.
#
# The analytics config lives in the committed mode files instead:
#
#   .env.production   `npm run build`            worldsoccersim.org
#   .env.itch         `npm run build:itch`       itch.io
#   .env.crazygames   `npm run build:crazygames` no key by design — that build
#                                                aliases posthog-js to a no-op
#
# They are committed because Vite inlines `import.meta.env.VITE_*` at build
# time, so the values must exist wherever the build runs, and every out-of-band
# place to keep them is a place they can be silently lost. They lived in the
# Vercel project; the 2026-08-15 move to Cloudflare left them behind and
# production shipped `posthog.init(undefined)` for five days without a single
# error, capturing nothing while looking healthy. See "Analytics & deploy
# config" in CLAUDE.md.
#
# What this file is still for: `npm run dev` runs in mode "development", which
# loads `.env` and `.env.development` — not `.env.production`. So a dev server
# reports nothing by default, which is usually what you want, since dev clicks
# would otherwise land in the same project as real players and count against
# the 1M-events/month free tier.
#
# Copy this to `.env` (gitignored) only if you deliberately want your local dev
# session to report. Remember to delete it afterwards.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_nqhYqPRCqWKbvbmWV4Nqs4NzmVP2xA8fUgtAMdGnF9FZ
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Verifying a real deploy, which is the check that would have caught the
# Cloudflare regression on day one:
#
#   curl -s https://worldsoccersim.org/assets/index-*.js | grep -c phc_
#
# Zero means that build went out with no key.

# The Import Custom League screen can offer a ready-made roster file as a
# download. It is off unless VITE_ROSTER_DOWNLOAD_URL is set, and it is set per
# build target rather than here — see .env.production for the reasoning, and
# .env.crazygames for why that one build leaves it off on purpose.
